# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Board overlay: Wireless-Tag WT-SC01 Plus. Overlays the root
# sdkconfig.defaults and wins on conflicts (composed in the root CMakeLists).
#
# The chip itself is NOT set here. IDF resolves IDF_TARGET in an early pass
# that cannot see -DBOARD, so a CONFIG_IDF_TARGET line here is read too late
# and silently loses. Select the chip the ordinary way:
#   idf.py -DBOARD=wt_sc01_plus set-target esp32s3
#
# Nothing is overridden yet, and the two things NOT set are the point of this
# file — both are traps, and both are cheaper to read than to rediscover:
#
#   PSRAM. Our unit is an N16R2: 2 MB of EMBEDDED QUAD PSRAM, measured with
#   esptool, not 8 MB octal. The Thermostat hit a different WT-SC01 Plus whose
#   module was octal-capable and boot-looped on the wrong line mode:
#     octal_psram: PSRAM chip is not connected, or wrong PSRAM line mode
#   so do not assume either size or mode from the silkscreen. PSRAM is left
#   disabled here — the panel demo runs out of internal RAM. Whoever turns it
#   on for LVGL framebuffers wants
#       CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
#       CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_QUAD=y
#   and should expect the drift guard to want a fresh sdkconfig afterwards.
#   2 MB is tight for double 480x320x2 framebuffers (600 KB) plus heap, so
#   check the numbers rather than assuming the Thermostat's 8 MB headroom.
#
#   FLASH SIZE. The bootloader detects 16 MB; the root defaults declare 4 MB and that
#   is deliberately left alone. partitions.csv ends at exactly 0x400000, so
#   nothing is lost, and raising it here would contradict a root default and
#   trip the sdkconfig drift guard in the root CMakeLists. Growing the flash
#   is a partition-table change first, and this line second.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── PSRAM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Now enabled, because LVGL plus the radio is a different memory budget from the
# colour-bar demo that preceded it. QUAD is measured, not assumed: esptool reports
# "Embedded PSRAM 2MB (AP_3v3)" for this unit (an S3R2). Getting the line mode
# wrong does not degrade, it boot-loops:
#   octal_psram: PSRAM chip is not connected, or wrong PSRAM line mode
#
# The LVGL draw buffers deliberately do NOT live here — they stay in internal DMA
# RAM (buff_dma, buff_spiram=false in UiManager). Rendering into PSRAM makes every
# redraw compete with the panel DMA for the same bus, which the Thermostat saw as
# on-screen artifacts. PSRAM is here for the general heap, not the hot path.
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_QUAD=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC=y

# ── Flash and partitions ───────────────────────────────────────
# 16 MB, and this board's own partition table with it. The shared partitions.csv
# said a per-board table buys nothing until the image outgrows 1.9 MB; it has,
# so this is that note coming due rather than a change of mind. See
# partitions_wt_sc01_plus.csv for the layout and why 8 MB of it is left blank.
#
# The retraction below is load-bearing. Flash size is a Kconfig CHOICE, so
# selecting 16MB sets a DIFFERENT key rather than overwriting the root's 4MB one
# — the root's assertion is not shadowed, it is falsified, and the drift guard
# would fire on a correctly configured tree. Retracting the arm we are leaving
# is the narrow, named way to say so; the 16MB line itself is still checked.
# STRUX_DRIFT_EXEMPT: CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_4MB
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_wt_sc01_plus.csv"

# ── LVGL fonts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Four sizes, because hierarchy on a 320x480 panel has to come from type and not
# only from colour: 14 for secondary lines, 16 for the primary line of a row, 20
# for screen titles, 28 for the wordmark on the home screen. Montserrat 14 alone
# is what LVGL ships with, and a UI drawn entirely in it reads flat no matter how
# the colours are arranged.
#
# About 60 KB of flash between them. That is affordable only because of the
# partition change above — it would have left the old 1.94 MB slot with a margin
# not worth having.
CONFIG_LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_14=y
CONFIG_LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_16=y
CONFIG_LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_20=y
CONFIG_LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_28=y

# ── Screenshots ───────────────────────────────────────
# lv_snapshot_take_to_draw_buf(), which is the whole of `ui screenshot`. Default n in
# LVGL's own Kconfig, so it has to be asked for. About 2 KB of flash, and it allocates
# nothing until a capture is asked for — the frame buffer is the caller's (UiManager
# takes it from PSRAM, not from LVGL's 64 KB lv_malloc pool).
CONFIG_LV_USE_SNAPSHOT=y
